# .version-scope — the paths whose version number is NOT this repo's release version.
#
# One path or path-prefix per line; `#` comments allowed. A prefix covers everything
# beneath it, so a whole helper tree is one line.
#
# Read it as a SCOPE, not as a mute switch. Every version-bearing file outside this
# list is expected to carry the number in CHANGELOG.md, and a file that disagrees is
# still an error — listing a path here says "this one was never on that axis", which
# is a different claim from "ignore this one".

# ── End-to-end test helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tools/e2e/ holds small standalone crates that exist only to drive the end-to-end
# connectivity runs. Each is its own cargo workspace, is never published to a
# registry, and is built only by the scenario it belongs to. Nothing depends on one,
# so there is nothing a version number on it could tell anybody.
#
# They are pinned at 0.0.0 — the usual way a Rust crate says "not versioned" — and
# that is deliberate. Tracking the browser's release number instead would mean these
# crates announced a version on every cut while nothing about them had changed, which
# is a number that means less than no number at all.
tools/e2e
